<title>UK: WH Smith to open 5 Hong Kong airport shops.</title>
<headline>WH Smith to open 5 Hong Kong airport shops.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retailer  W.H.Smith Group Plc said on Tuesday it had won a concession to operate five news and gift shops in the new Hong Kong airport, which is due to open next year.</p>
<p>Smiths will open four Waterstones book stores and one W.H. Smith outlet under a concession which runs for five years.</p>
<p>The airport had invited bids for 10 non-duty free shops, but stipulated that no single company could run more than six.</p>
<p>Smith's opened a Waterstone's in Singapore in 1995, which has performed very well, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Smiths also has airport shops in Britain and the United States.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom + 44 171 542 7717</p>
